       <property name="text">
        <string>Images can be manually corrected for scale using a spatial reference such as a ruler. For retrospective data, two, three, or four reference points can be used to apply the correction, where a four-point correction additionally accounts for perspective distortion. For prospective data, we recommand using our fiducial markers to automatically correct photographs. For more information please visit our wiki page.</string>
       </property>
